While the match loads, the client services the network from a thread of
its own whenever the loading has not polled for 100 ms. One loading step
can take 20 s on a slow disk (a champion with its forms on the MacBook):
with no acknowledgements ENet on the server doubled its resend waits to
tens of seconds, and when the server shortened the player's timeout at
the end of the loading it dropped the player at once (2 s into the
match, 2026-11-16). Packets wait in ENet's queue for poll(); every use of
the host is under one mutex. Any server, unchanged, keeps the player.

